Creation of Virtual Machine (Ubuntu EC2) & Deployment of Web App (index.html) Using AWS EC2

Step 1:
Open your course portal and click on Modules.

Step 2:
Scroll down and select Launch AWS Academy Lab.

Step 3:
Click Start Lab.

Step 4:
Open the AWS console → In Services, select EC2.
Launching an EC2 Instance

Step 5:
Go to Instances → click Launch Instance.

Step 6:
Enter the instance name:
➡️ week-122

Step 7:
Select the OS:
➡️ Ubuntu Server (latest LTS)

Step 8:
Architecture: 64-bit (x86)
Instance type: t3.micro (free-tier eligible)
Key Pair Creation

Step 9:
Click Create new key pair
Key pair type: RSA
File format: .pem
Click Create key pair (download will start)
Network Security Configuration

Step 10:
Under Network settings, choose:
Create security group
Security group name: (your choice)
Click Edit (top right) → Add rule:
Type	Port	Source
SSH	22	Anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)
This allows SSH connection.
Storage & Instance Count

Step 11:
Storage: 8 GB
Number of instances: 2
Click Launch Instance

Step 12:
Instances will start launching. A success message appears.

Step 13:
Go to Instances to see the created instances.
(Optional) Rename the instance:
➡️ “week-1222” → webapp
Connecting to EC2 via SSH

Step 14:
Select the instance → Click Connect → Choose SSH Client.
Copy the SSH command shown.

Step 15:
Open terminal → navigate to the folder where your .pem file exists.
Run the SSH command.
Install Docker & Git

Step 16:
Check version:
docker --version
git --version
If not installed:
sudo su
sudo apt-get update

Step 17: Install Docker:
sudo apt-get install docker.io
Clone Git Project & Build Docker Image

Step 18:
Clone your Git repository:
git clone <repo-url>
Enter the project folder:
cd <project-folder>

Step 19:
Check for Dockerfile:
If not present, create one:
nano Dockerfile
Build image:
sudo docker build -t img1 .

Step 20: Run Docker Container
sudo docker run -d -p 8081:8080 img1

Step 21: Check Images & Containers
sudo docker images
sudo docker ps

Step 22: Access the Web Application
Take your Public IP from EC2 instance, e.g.:
➡️ 13.222.21.231

Open in browser:
13.222.21.231:8081
